Package: llmsa
Type: Package
Title: Measurement System Analysis for Pipelines Built on Large Language Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Daniel Andreas", "Moj", , "daniel.moj2@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0008-1594-6065"))
Description: Treats a pipeline built on a large language model (LLM) as a
    measurement system and validates it with the tools that analytical
    laboratories already use: crossed precision studies with variance
    components (gauge repeatability and reproducibility), attribute
    agreement with kappa statistics, bias against a reference,
    Plackett-Burman screening of robustness against prompt and formatting
    perturbations, simulation-based planning of study size, Westgard-rule
    control charts for ongoing system suitability, and a reproducible
    validation report. The package is pipeline-agnostic: any backend that
    turns a prompt and a model identifier into a text response can be
    validated, and results produced elsewhere can be imported.
